    "summary": "A novelty effect: the lift fades to nothing within three weeks.",
    "explanation": "The overall +6.4% (p < 0.001) averages a big first-week spike with weeks where the effect is gone. The daily lift starts high and decays towards zero, and the last week alone shows +0.9%, which cannot be told apart from no effect. Shipping on the average would promise a gain that has already disappeared. The split, the sample and the guardrail are fine; the trap is the pattern over time.",
    "issueNotes": {
      "novelty": "The lift was +15.2% in the first week and +0.9% in the last (p = 0.720). The daily lift falls steadily: users reacted to something new, not to something better."
    },
    "recommendation": "Do not ship. The lasting effect is about zero, and a streak adds complexity to every screen it touches. If the team believes in habits, test another mechanic, such as automatic weekly transfers, and judge it on its last weeks rather than its average.",
